From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO for Windows: Fire button

The Fire button of the Android app (CromIKO-Fire-Button.patch) on the
desktop: "Burn tabs and data" in the app menu, below "New Incognito
window", with the CromIKO fire icon (drawn from the logo by
tools/cromiko/gen_feature_icons.py).

It asks first, with Cancel as the default button. Then it closes all tabs
and windows of the profile, also its incognito windows, without keeping
them in Recent tabs, deletes the browsing history, cookies, site data and
cached files of all time (the history stays when a policy does not allow
deleting it, as in "Delete browsing data") and leaves one window with a new
tab. When the data is deleted, a toast says "All clean!".

